                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Repackaged games like this are one of main reasons for why I believe copyright terms should not last longer than thirty years for works-for-hire.  There is nothing you get out of this deal you wouldn’t get emulating the game through other means.  If we ignore that and say this is the best legal way to experience the game, by patronizing a company that had nothing to do with its creation, THEN is it worth it?\n\nNo.  The player character moves too slow, the environments have only a couple decent setpieces to break up the dark, repetitive levels, and the combat doesn’t feel remotely tactile.  No impact, no sound effects, and an overreliance on the jump attack.  It’s not too difficult; you won’t need the save states to beat this in a day, because even when it kicks you back to the title screen, “game start” brings you back to your last checkpoint.\n\nExpand the public domain, crack down on IP parasites, don’t buy this game.",
